 "provenance_note": "R26-306 intake (2026-09-24). Tier PLAUSIBLE: the GDP denominator is a primary dataset on disk (CONFIRMED), but the railway numerator is Odlyzko's secondary reproduction of Mitchell (1988), whose primary is not on disk; a series takes its weakest figure's tier (E99 s93: a PLAUSIBLE page may draw, its source line saying what it is). The numerator is the year's INCREASE IN CUMULATIVE INVESTED CAPITAL, not construction spending: Odlyzko's own Fig. 2 (construction investment) peaks at about £44M in 1847 - 7.0% of the BoE GDP (44 / 628.29) - and his text rounds it to 7.3% of £600M. So the peak reads 6.5-7.3% by measure; the chart says 6.5% because that is the arithmetic of its own series, and the script may say 'about 7%'. Every one of the Gemini reply's UK rows is REJECTED (see VERIFY.md): its DOIs do not resolve or resolve to other books, and its GDP column contradicts the BoE dataset (1847: £465M vs £628M). The US 1850s-1870s series is not drawn (no retrievable annual current-dollar source; the reply's citations misresolve)."
